BLOCKDEV(8)                  System Administration                 BLOCKDEV(8)



NNAAMMEE
       blockdev - call block device ioctls from the command line

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       bblloocckkddeevv [--qq] [--vv] _c_o_m_m_a_n_d [_c_o_m_m_a_n_d...] _d_e_v_i_c_e [_d_e_v_i_c_e...]

       bblloocckkddeevv ----rreeppoorrtt [_d_e_v_i_c_e...]

       bblloocckkddeevv --hh|--VV

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The utility bblloocckkddeevv allows one to call block device ioctls from the
       command line.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --qq
           Be quiet.

       --vv
           Be verbose.

       ----rreeppoorrtt
           Print a report for the specified device. It is possible to give
           multiple devices. If none is given, all devices which appear in
           _/_p_r_o_c_/_p_a_r_t_i_t_i_o_n_s are shown. Note that the partition StartSec is in
           512-byte sectors.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

CCOOMMMMAANNDDSS
       It is possible to give multiple devices and multiple commands.

       ----fflluusshhbbuuffss
           Flush buffers.

       ----ggeettaalliiggnnooffff
           Get alignment offset.

       ----ggeettbbsszz
           Print the blocksize in bytes. This size does not describe device
           topology. It’s the size used internally by the kernel and it may be
           modified (for example) by filesystem driver on mount.

       ----ggeettddiissccaarrddzzeerrooeess
           Get discard zeroes support status.

       ----ggeettffrraa
           Get filesystem readahead in 512-byte sectors.

       ----ggeettiioommiinn
           Get minimum I/O size.

       ----ggeettiioooopptt
           Get optimal I/O size.

       ----ggeettmmaaxxsseecctt
           Get max sectors per request.

       ----ggeettppbbsszz
           Get physical block (sector) size.

       ----ggeettrraa
           Print readahead (in 512-byte sectors).

       ----ggeettrroo
           Get read-only. Print 1 if the device is read-only, 0 otherwise.

       ----ggeettssiizzee6644
           Print device size in bytes.

       ----ggeettssiizzee
           Print device size (32-bit!) in sectors. Deprecated in favor of the
           ----ggeettsszz option.

       ----ggeettssss
           Print logical sector size in bytes - usually 512.

       ----ggeettsszz
           Get size in 512-byte sectors.

       ----rreerreeaaddpptt
           Reread partition table

       ----sseettbbsszz _b_y_t_e_s
           Set blocksize. Note that the block size is specific to the current
           file descriptor opening the block device, so the change of block
           size only persists for as long as bblloocckkddeevv has the device open, and
           is lost once bblloocckkddeevv exits.

       ----sseettffrraa _s_e_c_t_o_r_s
           Set filesystem readahead (same as ----sseettrraa on 2.6 kernels).

       ----sseettrraa _s_e_c_t_o_r_s
           Set readahead (in 512-byte sectors).

       ----sseettrroo
           Set read-only. The currently active access to the device may not be
           affected by the change. For example, a filesystem already mounted
           in read-write mode will not be affected. The change applies after
           remount.

       ----sseettrrww
           Set read-write.

